\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. The head that once was crowned with thorns
\par Is crowned with glory now;
\par A royal diadem adorns
\par The mighty victor's brow.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. The highest place that heaven affords
\par Is His, is His by right,
\par The king of kings and Lord of lords,
\par And heavens eternal light.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. The joy of all who dwell above,
\par The joy of all below
\par To whom He manifests His love,
\par And grants His name to know.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. To them the cross, with all its shame,
\par With all its grace, is given,
\par Their name an everlasting name,
\par Their joy the joy of heaven.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. They suffer with their Lord below,
\par They reign with Him above,
\par Their profit and their joy to know
\par The mystery of His love.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. The cross He bore is life and health,
\par Though shame and death to Him;
\par His peoples hope, His people's wealth,
\par Their everlasting theme.
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

